agsdict:GCHM
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary> ;
    skos:altLabel "GCHM"@en ;
    skos:definition "Geotechnical Chemistry Testing"@en ;
    skos:historyNote """Group status: This group is reserved for soil/water chemistry testing associated with geotechnical design assessments. Environmental contamination testing should be recorded in Group ELRG
AGS 4.1: Headings Added - SPEC_BASE, GCHM_DEV, GCHM_SGRP, GCHM_LSID, GCHM_RDEV, GCHM_RDAT, GCHM_DTIM, GCHM_TEST, GCHM_IREF, GCHM_ITYP
AGS 4.1: Group Rule Added - • Where a reading has no unit, the GCHM_UNIT data shall be set to 'UNITLESS' • Units included in GCHM_UNIT shall be fully defined in the UNIT group (Rule 15), the unit group is case sensitive. • Data type for data field heading GCHM_UNIT shall not be changed from PU.""" ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary> ;
    skos:narrower
        agsdict:FILE_FSET ,
        agsdict:GCHM_CODE ,
        agsdict:GCHM_CRED ,
        agsdict:GCHM_DEV ,
        agsdict:GCHM_DLM ,
        agsdict:GCHM_DTIM ,
        agsdict:GCHM_IREF ,
        agsdict:GCHM_ITYP ,
        agsdict:GCHM_LAB ,
        agsdict:GCHM_LSID ,
        agsdict:GCHM_METH ,
        agsdict:GCHM_NAME ,
        agsdict:GCHM_PERP ,
        agsdict:GCHM_RDAT ,
        agsdict:GCHM_REM ,
        agsdict:GCHM_RESL ,
        agsdict:GCHM_RTXT ,
        agsdict:GCHM_SGRP ,
        agsdict:GCHM_SIZE ,
        agsdict:GCHM_TEST ,
        agsdict:GCHM_TTYP ,
        agsdict:GCHM_UNIT ,
        agsdict:LOCA_ID ,
        agsdict:SAMP_ID ,
        agsdict:SAMP_REF ,
        agsdict:SAMP_TOP ,
        agsdict:SAMP_TYPE ,
        agsdict:SPEC_BASE ,
        agsdict:SPEC_DESC ,
        agsdict:SPEC_DPTH ,
        agsdict:SPEC_PREP ,
        agsdict:SPEC_REF ,
        agsdict:TEST_STAT ;
    skos:notation "GCHM"^^xsd:token ;
    skos:prefLabel "Geotechnical Chemistry Testing"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote
        """GCHM_RDEV included in error in AGS 4.1.0 Dec 2020, this heading shall not be used and shall be regarded as deleted. Correct heading is GCHM_DEV.
GCHM is used to report chemical testing carried out for geotechnical design and shall not be transferred or duplicated within ELRG.
GCHM is to be used for testing in accordance with BS 1377, BS EN 1744-1+A1, testing for use in the assessment described in BRE Special Digest 1 and/or buried steel testing described in the Design Manual for Roads and Bridges; CD 375. Chemical testing for contamination or water quality testing is reported in ELRG. Laboratory resistivity test results should be reported using the LRES Group.
The GCHM_CODE abbreviations to report testing to BRE Special Digest 1 and BS 1377-3 would be:
PH = Acidity/alkalinity (pH value to nearest 0.1)
WS = Water-soluble sulfate (as mg/l SO4)
AS = Acid-soluble sulfate (as % SO4)
TS = Total sulfur (as % S)
WMG = Water/soil extract Magnesium (as mg/l)
NH4 = Ammonium ion (as mg/l)
CL = Chloride (as mg/l)
NO3 = Nitrate (as mg/l)
ACO2 = Aggressive Carbon dioxide (as mg/l)
CO2 = Carbonate content (as %CO2)
LOI = Loss on ignition (as %)
OGM = Organic matter content (as %)
TDS = Total dissolved solids (in mg/l to 2SF)
CACO3 = Chalk content (as %CaCO3)
The GCHM_CODE abbreviations to report testing of buried steel would be:
REDOX = Redox Potential (as mV)
All GCHM_CODE abbreviations reported in this group are to be listed in the ABBR group.
The GCHM_TTYP abbreviations would be limited to SOLID_21WAT, SOLID_ACID, SOLID_TOT and WATER to report testing to BRE Special Digest 1 and BS 1377-3.
GCHM_UNIT is a REQUIRED field (Rule 10b) which enforces the inclusion of units for all test results. Where a test result has no unit, the GCHM_UNIT data shall be set to "UNITLESS".
Units reported in GCHM_UNIT must be fully defined in the UNIT group (Rule 15). It is possible that units require conversion when the data is received and amalgamated into project databases to ensure that data are consistent across testing tranches and appropriate for the assessment.
For a chalk content test carried out to BS1377-3, it would be good practice to report both a Carbonate content (as CO2) and the chalk content (as %CaCO3)."""@en ,
        """Group rules: Where a reading has no unit, the GCHM_UNIT data shall be set to "UNITLESS".
Units included in GCHM_UNIT shall be fully defined in the UNIT group (Rule 15), the unit group is case sensitive.
Data type for data field heading GCHM_UNIT shall not be changed from PU."""@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://gitlab.com/AGS-DFWG-Web/ASG4/-/blob/710b1f08097264e6508be1397282aece79278fc4/AGS4/AGS4_2/4_2_0/groupsandheadings4-2-0.json> ;
    schema:status status:stable ;
    agso:groupClass ags:GCHM ;
    agso:parentGroup agsdict:SAMP ;
.

